RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
2026-08-16: Read the immutable evaluator, starter contract, all repository-memory sections, sibling study-outcome claim, and prior temporal protocol. Profiled task origins, target lattice, exact target-event query, event multiplicity, and cutoff-visible roster coverage; recorded the findings in measurement_profile.md and the critical-path schedule in PLAN.md.
2026-08-16: Implemented the target-exact semiannual replay, cutoff-safe all-table trial and facility feature engines, sampled reporting and exact-success LightGBM heads, supervised TF-IDF head, conditional ratio-lattice median DP, large-roster Monte Carlo tail, direct facility L1 fallback, connected-component bootstrap, and required slice diagnostics.
2026-08-16: Executed a hosted OpenAI methodology-judgment probe and 512-trial batch with pinned model gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17. Responses are cached by model, prompt version, origin, structured context, and complete-document hash under lane0_hosted_judgments_v1; the 148-row forward panel measured AUC 0.570868 and MAE 0.494435 before the snapshot block.
2026-08-16: Materialized cutoff-safe AACT archives from https://aact.ctti-clinicaltrials.org/static/static_db_copies/daily/<snapshot-date>?source=web. Snapshot 2017-06-13 SHA256 6dff60cfe80684157c2c072238945851c8cfb3f29e4a0a07c1d893c26353969c; 2017-12-17 866a9d38df183788fb20db57bae0ddef83c2963a7bf95b2fd15011189af9a42b; 2018-06-01 f13182b5a8cb42c3e8700dbd8d1e7f59e1b33e0c07c14b896f623ad402523d69; 2018-12-01 8590ca2c0767957b2fc7b1bf8283c18891aa15ef7288c62cf54755ca153a2212; 2019-12-01 c56c06707fa77786229f3c745771bbc747ba304a32601085988bedb9c5442909; 2020-12-01 d44da0ac916022efb876089dc7e8a7bb698e8d0db72211be184bc90426868405. Each archive is strictly earlier than its mapped origin; no snapshot at or after an origin is read.
2026-08-16: Added registry status, completion clocks and revisions, results submission/QC/posting state, pending-event recency, why-stopped state, facility changes, and sponsor reporting delay. The corrected exact direct-evidence rule covered 5.18%/4.59% of reporting trials in the 2018/2019 gates and measured expert MAE 0.0050/0.0252; poles were enabled only after both gates passed.
2026-08-16: Banked run_0001 at official validation MAE 0.3338116559 without snapshots and run_0002 at 0.3184141962 with snapshots. The run_0002 most-shifted forward MAEs were 0.345536 in 2018 and 0.262723 in 2019; the conditional lattice median beat its conditional-mean and direct-L1 report-only comparators.
2026-08-16: Began the supervised answerdotai/ModernBERT-large exact-success gate with complete-document 4,096-token windowing, two BF16 epochs, learning rate 2e-5, weight decay 0.01, and effective batch 32. An eight-document single-GPU microbatch failed at 39.30 GiB with torch.OutOfMemoryError; gradient checkpointing plus four documents per assigned GPU resolved the allocation failure while preserving effective batch size.
2026-08-16: The ModernBERT checkpoint completed in 1,107.8 seconds. Its 2019 reporting-trial panel measured AUC 0.625524 versus 0.695361 tabular and 0.672072 TF-IDF; a 10% encoder blend added only 0.000212 AUC over the best no-encoder blend, below the connected-trial acceptance threshold, so encoder inference was rejected and its cached predictions were retained.
2026-08-16: Compared equal-trial, success-only square-root/full-site, and joint square-root/full-site weighting in run_0004. Equal-trial remained selected at forward MAE 0.312805/0.256389 for 2018/2019; success-only square-root weighting worsened these to at best 0.379384/0.273678, so subsequent runs freeze equal weighting. Direct exact-evidence poles explain the forward improvement versus run_0002 while producing an identical frozen Model A checksum and official MAE 0.3184141962.
2026-08-16: Tested 162 within-origin percentile, robust-z, and leader-gap transforms for snapshot numeric fields in run_0005. The block worsened 2019 forward MAE from 0.256389 to 0.272766 and official report-only MAE from 0.3184141962 to 0.3248414090, so it was removed from the active pipeline.
2026-08-16: Tested roster-presence thresholds 0.05/0.10/0.20/0.35 plus rich- and dormant-history facility-L1 routers in run_0006. None beat the conditional lattice median on the 2018/2019 gate; the selected checksum and official MAE remained identical to run_0004, so lattice decoding remains frozen.
2026-08-16: The first quarterly debug rebuild showed 183 base columns rather than the cached 178 because the categorical completeness loop emitted five all-missing registry placeholders. Snapshot attachment previously skipped same-named columns, which would silently discard real statuses on a fresh cache. Fixed attachment to overwrite placeholders from the verified registry matrix before any full quarterly run.
2026-08-16: Rescored and verified archived run_0002 at MAE 0.31841419621347. Its immutable val/test SHA256 values remain 90450055d04a3ad6a57267b33a35ee297f0de3e7e0e25e6589bf9bd1a18d9ae4 and 4c1710c1a9830d0cb7500bdbc1e9fe39108f14ab765d32a17bf473ce6884c616, with candidate code, manifest, selection record, vectors, diagnostics, and Model-A lineage retained in the run archive and registered shared artifact.
2026-08-16: Consumed and specifically registered the READY target_exact_quarterly_v3 artifact bcd3d8470814da67 without rebuilding it. Its 183,321 shared semiannual replay rows have identical report and success labels; it expands coverage to 706,991 pairs and 358,010 replay rows at 58,301 feature rows/minute.
2026-08-16: Added 68,206 missing 2017 trial-origin feature rows and 311,481 physical-as-of roster edges, then expanded quarterly replay into 4,117,586 monthly at-risk rows. Implemented the 12-bin LightGBM hazard, archived OOF hazard shapes, conditional reporter-subset likelihood with six roster covariates and ridge/boundary selection, exact-to-32 lattice DP, deterministic 8,192-draw tail decoding, 2,000-draw paired connected-component gates, slice reporting, and a cross-fitted quantile meta-median gate.
2026-08-16: Fixed a forward-ruler bug discovered in debug: _pair_rows_for_year selected every quarterly trial-origin row in a calendar year rather than the exact January 1 origin. Versioned and rebuilt all hazard OOF folds after restricting it to the physical forecast origin.
2026-08-16: Full monthly gate selected 800 rounds and ridge 10. Hazard marginal reporting was rejected on 2019 (AUC 0.859503 versus binary 0.870079; facility MAE 0.288761 versus 0.277028; Gate A P=0.0575). Conditional recalibration improved raw hazard to 0.278741 with P=0.8665 but failed Gate C versus binary at P=0.259; the rich/recent meta-router also failed at P=0.0095 and was not used. The 8,192-draw audit matched exact lattice medians on 98.44% of 64 rosters and had 0.003904 mean error for the conditional mean.
2026-08-16: Executed the required hosted text measurement over 512 quarterly trials, including 293 new schema-valid calls at 14.92 rows/s. Its forward panel measured AUC 0.534392 and MAE 0.497607, so the text judgment block remains diagnostic rather than entering the reporting system.
2026-08-16: Full Model A was frozen before any 2020 labels entered fitting; Model B alone added 2020 monthly outcomes and facility labels. The structurally different validation vector has SHA256 af51ffe072245d33865ffa1f779230f1eeee306b40708602acebb3a2818c95b2 and report-only MAE 0.3137501544; its forward Gate C rejection remains the honest selection result despite the flat-origin improvement.
2026-08-16: Registered full evaluation archived run_0007 with official validation R2 -0.0960373166, MAE 0.3137501544, and RMSE 0.5001064325 under evaluator e9d1efaa0b5fd4ac0891eb083b9fe653560755415c2a0516814af5fe06e3a408. The evaluation tree remained byte-unchanged.
2026-08-16: Resolution follow-up measured candidate/incumbent Spearman 0.790832, mean absolute prediction difference 0.129542, candidate connected-component MAE SE 0.040500, and paired P(improvement)=0.594 over 500 draws. The 2019 forward ruler rejects the candidate while flat 2020 prefers it, confirming that the single official origin does not reliably order these candidates.
2026-08-16: Completed the specified equal/2/4/6-year hazard half-life selection using 2017-2018 OOF log loss. Two years won the training-period criterion, but on the once-opened 2019 gate raw/conditional facility MAE were 0.288796/0.281868 and Gate C P(improvement over binary)=0.083, worse than equal weighting's 0.288761/0.278741/P=0.259. Retained equal weighting and stopped the rejected two-year candidate before its unneeded Model A/B refit; all six selection fits and its 2019 vector remain cached.
2026-08-16: Tested a low-capacity 10% hazard-logit / 90% binary-logit reporting hybrid selected on 2017-2018 log loss. It raised 2019 reporting AUC from 0.870079 to 0.872847 and reduced conditional facility MAE from binary 0.277028 to 0.276511, but paired Gate C reached only P=0.626 and Gate B reached 0.751. Rejected it under the 0.8 gate and stopped its final Model A/B refit; no second official evaluation was run.
2026-08-16: Audited the conditional likelihood after the first archive and found that seed_row is origin-local, so concatenated 2017-2019 calibration frames had merged unrelated facility rosters. Added a year-qualified roster_key, regenerated every conditional and meta gate, and superseded the earlier conditional-recalibration readings while retaining the unchanged hazard-head measurements.
2026-08-16: Added an analytically checked conditional-likelihood gradient (SciPy check_grad error 3.81e-08) and repeated boundary extension through intercept ranges +/-2, +/-4, +/-8, and +/-12. The corrected training-period selection chose ridge 10; its frozen Model-A intercept 8.0000 and temperature 0.31167 are interior to the final [-12,12] and [0.05,20] ranges.
2026-08-16: With correct roster identities, 2019 conditional MAE improved from raw hazard 0.288761 and binary 0.277028 to 0.269534. Gate B reached P=0.9545 and completed-system Gate C reached P=0.8875 over 2,000 paired connected-component draws; the rich/recent meta-router remained rejected at P=0.0235. Model A stayed free of 2020 labels and produced report-only validation MAE 0.310346 with checksum c4d28afb2249efe5e0c8f3612f15a2b54bbbea27cf95dbf6e02a5c6d43ddcdd3 before registered scoring.
